the same COMDAT difference: cl inlines the closures away and emits no symbol for their copy constructors, destructors or call operators, where cxx1 emits a real function for each. Every difference is a name cxx1 has and cl has none of. What this case is about - that a by-copy capture of a class calls its copy constructor and is destroyed with the closure, and that a captured array is copied rather than decayed - is checked by run-cases.cmd on the box and by the ledger line in its .expected, and the closure names cxx1 does write carry their enclosing function correctly. lambda-capture-by-value.nonames records the clang side of the same thing.
